response.text:
The `parseRange` function was failing for single-value ranges (e.g., `"7"`) because it split the string by `"-"` and attempted to convert the resulting `undefined` second element to a number, resulting in `NaN`. I updated the function to use the starting value as the ending value when no hyphen is present.

```javascript
export function parseRange(text) {
  const [from, to] = text.split("-");
  const fromNum = Number(from);
  return { from: fromNum, to: to === undefined ? fromNum : Number(to) };
}
```
